	Uh, why's that? Magicbane has some useful properties (the curse
catching, mainly), and is a pretty decent weapon in the early game when
the random bonus damage is more effective than doubling enchantment
bonuses that you probably don't have yet, but as an actual melee weapon
in the mid-to-late game, it's pretty crappy. My two wizard ascensions
used Fire Brand and Stormbringer, respectively, as their primary melee
weapons for most of the game, switching to Magicbane only when getting
cursed seemed likely.

	Of course, the problem becomes that the part of the game where a
wizard most needs a melee weapon - the ascension run, where the bursty
nature of the fighting and the Amulet's Power-draining effect make
casting as a primary offense iffy, even with the Eye - is also the part
of the game where you most need to be wielding Magicbane to catch random
curses.

